title: 'scripts/podcheck.pl: pre-weave source POD check for the [@Author::GETTY] weaver
  directives'
updated: 2026-09-18T23:02:12Z
---

Plain podchecker on a source .pm trips over the weaver directives (=attr/=method/=synopsis...) as 'Unknown directive', and on L</...> links into them as 'unresolved', because those become standard POD only after Pod::Weaver at build time -- which is why the canonical check (PodSyntaxTests/Test::Pod) runs against the built dist. podcheck.pl applies the same directive->head mapping in memory (line-for-line, so error lines still point at source) then runs Pod::Checker, so source POD and dead internal links (which Test::Pod never checks) can be verified without a full dzil build.

